  "description": "<p>\n\n\n\t<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Description:</span> This is a very small infrared receiver based on the TSOP85 receiver from Vishay. This receiver has all the filtering and 38kHz demodulation built into the unit. Simply point a IR remote at the receiver, hit a button, and you&#39;ll see a stream of 1s and 0s out of the data pin.<br />\n\n\n\t<br />\n\n\n\t<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Documents:</span></p>\n\n\n<ul>\n\n\n\t<li>\n\n\n\t\t<a classname=\"\" href=\"http://www.sparkfun.com/datasheets/Sensors/Infrared/tsop853.pdf\" name=\"\" target=\"_blank\">Datasheet</a></li>\n\n\n\t<li>\n\n\n\t\t<a href=\"http://www.sparkfun.com/datasheets/Sensors/Infrared/IR-Receiver-Schematic.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Schematic</a></li>\n\n\n\t<li>\n\n\n\t\t<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consumer_IR\" target=\"_blank\">Consumer IR Information</a></li>\n\n\n</ul>",
